Tournament Analysis vignettes (oracle-2026-06-01-S24)

============================================================
(1) BASKETBALL — pass matrix -> tournament of 5
============================================================
 Team A (PG-heavy): score=(1, 1, 2, 2, 4)  H=5  ties_via_path=0
 Team B (with ties): score=(1, 2, 2, 2, 3)  H=13  ties_via_path=5
 The team is a POINT in G_5; a season is a walk (one point per game).
 Note H=1 would mean a perfect passing pecking-order (transitive);
 higher H means cyclic passing structure (no clean hierarchy).

============================================================
(2) H as a spread-meter over the runner clock
============================================================
 [arith 0..4]
    H=1  : cells=2   max_gap in [0.750, 0.750]  mean=0.750
    H=9  : cells=2   max_gap in [0.417, 0.417]  mean=0.417
    H=11 : cells=4   max_gap in [0.292, 0.292]  mean=0.292
    H=15 : cells=4   max_gap in [0.208, 0.312]  mean=0.260
 [primes 0,2,3,5,7]
    H=1  : cells=8   max_gap in [0.536, 0.750]  mean=0.605
    H=9  : cells=4   max_gap in [0.400, 0.464]  mean=0.432
    H=11 : cells=16  max_gap in [0.268, 0.414]  mean=0.353
    H=15 : cells=4   max_gap in [0.225, 0.304]  mean=0.264
 [spread 0,1,4,9,11]
    H=1  : cells=18  max_gap in [0.523, 0.750]  mean=0.555
    H=9  : cells=34  max_gap in [0.364, 0.477]  mean=0.436
    H=11 : cells=24  max_gap in [0.335, 0.442]  mean=0.399
    H=15 : cells=4   max_gap in [0.267, 0.351]  mean=0.309

 Trend: H=1 (transitive) sits at the LARGEST gaps (>1/2, bunched);
 the maximal H (regular) sits at the SMALLEST max-gap (even spread).
 So H reads off how bunched the runners are — a tournament gap-meter.
